>197</fpage><lpage>200</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1545721</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Richards</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Ferrall</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Inappropriate use of emergency medical services transport: comparison of provider and patient perspectives</article-title><source>Acad Emerg Med</source><year>1999</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>14</fpage><lpage>20</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9928971</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Billittier</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Moscati</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Janicke</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Lerner</surname><given-names>EB</given-names></name><name><surname>Seymour</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Olsson</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A multisite survey of factors contributing to medically unnecessary ambulance transports</article-title><source>Acad Emerg Med</source><year>1996</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>1046</fpage><lpage>1052</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8922014</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gardner</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The use and abuse of the emergency ambulance service: some of the factors affecting the decision whether to call an emergency ambulance</article-title><source>Arch Emerg Med</source><year>1990</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>81</fpage><lpage>89</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2390158</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="a